{
 "about": "The material lab's third woods, the timber pass's finish (Sean's notes of 2026-10-14 on the timber pass: posts a little too clean, the fascia too big flat and pale, the paint wear a strip on every board, the red too bright and orange in low sun). lab2's parameters (woods_lab2.json's about) and: `knots` [min, max] a board; `weather` [amount, streak width m, length m] long dark streaks down the grain; `grey` [amount, patch m] sun-bleached toward grey; `saw_patchy` saw marks in patches, unevenly spaced; `check_lip` a lighter lifted lip above each split; `stain` [amount, height share] splash darkening toward the lower edge; `end_rim` the cut end's outer texels darker; painted woods `wear_local` (no edge strip: a few short broken runs of worn lap edge, some nails, `flakes` [min, max] patches flaking along the grain) and `end_wear` (m: the shader wears paint to `<wood>_bare.png` near each board's ends). `saloon_red_low` and `store_boards_low`: the same paint below ~1 m (LabGeometry gives the lowest boards them), splashed and worn more. `fascia`: the boardwalk's rim board.",
